This file turns GitHub Pages' Jekyll build off for the whole site, so that what is in this repository is byte for byte what is served. The reason is /babelfish/ and /licence/: signatures are checked over exact bytes, and a file transformed on its way to the web is a file that fails to verify on every customer's machine at once. It also stops Jekyll's readme-index plugin turning the README.md in either of those folders into a public page at /babelfish/ or /licence/. Nothing on this site has ever used Jekyll - every page is plain HTML with no front matter - so removing this file would change nothing about the marketing pages and would quietly reintroduce both problems above.
